1
00:05:40,909 --> 00:05:46,909
She makes dinner. She does windows. She reads bedtime
stories. She's a blessing... in disguise.

2
00:11:21,818 --> 00:11:27,818
Mrs. Doubtfire is a comedy, drama, family film directed by Chris Columbus.

3
00:17:02,727 --> 00:17:08,727
Loving but irresponsible dad Daniel Hillard, estranged from his exasperated spouse, is
crushed by a court order allowing only weekly visits with his kids.

4
00:22:43,636 --> 00:22:49,636
When Daniel learns his ex needs a housekeeper, he gets
the job -- disguised as a British nanny.

5
00:28:24,545 --> 00:28:30,545
Soon he becomes not only his children's best pal but the kind
of parent he should have been from the start.

6
00:34:05,454 --> 00:34:11,454
Daniel Hillard / Mrs. Doubtfire, played by Robin Williams.

7
00:39:46,363 --> 00:39:52,363
Miranda Hillard, played by Sally Field.

8
00:45:27,272 --> 00:45:33,272
Lydia Hillard, played by Lisa Jakub.

9
00:51:08,181 --> 00:51:14,181
Chris Hillard, played by Matthew Lawrence.

10
00:56:49,090 --> 00:56:55,090
Natalie Hillard, played by Mara Wilson.

11
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:36,000
Stu, played by Pierce Brosnan.

12
01:08:10,909 --> 01:08:16,909
Doubtfire is a 1993 American comedy-drama film directed by Chris Columbus, written by Randi Mayem
Singer and Leslie Dixon, based on the 1987 novel Madame Doubtfire, by Anne Fine.

13
01:13:51,818 --> 01:13:57,818
The film was produced by Mark Radcliffe, Marsha Garces Williams and her
then-husband Robin Williams, who also starred in the lead role.

14
01:19:32,727 --> 01:19:38,727
The film co-stars Sally Field, Pierce Brosnan,
Harvey Fierstein, and Robert Prosky.

15
01:25:13,636 --> 01:25:19,636
It follows a recently divorced voice actor who disguises himself as an elderly
female housekeeper in order to spend time with his children.

16
01:30:54,545 --> 01:31:00,545
Doubtfire was released in the United States by 20th
Century Fox on November 24, 1993.

17
01:36:35,454 --> 01:36:41,454
It grossed $441.3 million on a $25 million budget, making it the
second-highest-grossing film of 1993 behind Jurassic Park.

18
01:42:16,363 --> 01:42:22,363
While critical reception was mixed, the film won the Academy Award for Best Makeup,
and the Golden Globe Award for Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy.

19
01:47:57,272 --> 01:48:03,272
Williams was awarded the Golden Globe Award for Best Actor
in a Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy.

20
01:53:38,181 --> 01:53:44,181
The film explores themes of mask, parent child relationship, san
francisco, california, social worker, transvestite.

21
01:59:19,090 --> 01:59:25,090
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
